WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.029
This next clip is sort of funny, but it's
also it's also kind of sad.

00:00:04.029 --> 00:00:06.870
I don't know why I kind of got bummed out
watching it.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.440
Dr. Anthony Fauci was on CNN yesterday with
Wolf Blitzer and Wolf Blitzer tried to make

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.610
a baseball analogy to the pandemic.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.900
And the analogy was, Dr. Fauci, you like baseball?

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.240
I like baseball.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.040
If this pandemic were a baseball game, what
inning would we be in?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:31.949
And Dr. Fauci just seeming exhausted, saying,
you know, Wolf, this isn't like baseball,

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:36.980
but I actually think there is a baseball analogy
that could be made that Dr. Fauci could use

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:38.019
in the future.

00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:39.109
I'll tell you in a second.

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:40.719
But let's take a look at the clip.

00:00:40.719 --> 00:00:46.469
Are we Dr. Fauci is a country right now in
our fight against this virus?

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:48.819
We're both baseball fans, for example.

00:00:48.819 --> 00:00:51.469
What inning are we in?

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:57.190
You know you know, it's not like baseball,
Wolf, because the inning that we're in is

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:59.840
going to depend on how we respond.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.390
And that's the issue because I mean, if I
say we're in the seventh inning, it's almost

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.780
over and we have surges like we're seeing
throughout Europe and the rest of the world.

00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:14.660
And the threat of a surge that we're seeing
now, you know, it's not measured in innings

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:15.660
anymore.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.420
It's measured on what we do to contain this.

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:24.090
OK, so Dr. Fauci is correct in the sense that
we're only in the seventh inning.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:29.250
If people behave one way and otherwise, it
might really only be like the fourth inning

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.009
or the fifth inning and we have a long way
to go.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:36.590
Here is me workshopping a better baseball
analogy.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:38.460
Tell me what you think about this.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.460
You know, Wolf, the pandemic isn't a game.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:46.929
It's really like a World Series where you
have to win four games to actually win.

00:01:46.929 --> 00:01:54.010
So the question is, are we going to sweep
this in four or is it going to go seven because

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.159
we don't finish off the virus as quickly as
we could.

00:01:57.159 --> 00:01:58.159
Right.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:01:59.159
That's the baseball analogy.

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:04.659
What I can tell you, Wolf, is we have one
more game to win, but will it be a sweep or

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:06.560
will this go seven games?

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:07.560
Right.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.940
You could maybe you could even go further.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:17.230
Game one, testing and controlling the spread
game to scaling up testing and researching

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:18.230
vaccines.

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:23.470
Game three, developing and testing the vaccines
game for finishing vaccination to end the

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.470
pandemic.

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.840
And then next year, you might have another
World Series, right.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.040
Variants, potentially new vaccines.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.320
The other baseball analogy I was thinking
of that might work would be listen, Wolf.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:41.520
We're in the seventh inning, but the virus
is trying to catch up, and if they do and

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.030
and we have a tie, then we go extra innings.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.540
And as you know, Wolf, extra innings can go
on indefinitely until someone wins.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:56.040
And we don't want that every time a red state
doesn't have enough people wanting the vaccine.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.220
The virus has just knocked in a single.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.510
If the virus gets enough of these singles,
it's going to start putting runs up on the

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.510
board.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.140
My going too far with this.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:10.470
Regardless, we all share Dr. Falsies exhaustion
with this.

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:17.710
If it's game four and you can finish it off
or have to play another game, you power through

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:18.760
the exhaustion.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.340
And that's what we're hopefully doing with
three and a half million vaccinations a day.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.560
We're going to have to deal with the pause
on the Johnson and Johnson vaccine over the

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.990
blood clot fears, as I told you earlier.

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:31.990
But big picture.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:38.100
I mean, do you think it's a problem that Wolf
Blitzer and others use these whether it's

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.940
sports analogies or whatever the case may
be like?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:47.230
On one hand, there really is no analogy to
something with a defined duration because

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:49.670
the duration is is whatever we make it.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.510
New Zealand, just stop this.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.880
You could say they walked off the field after
the first inning and said we don't have to

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:58.040
play the rest of the game because there's
almost nothing left to do.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.040
They controlled it so.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.040
Well, I don't know.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.030
I don't know if maybe the sports analogies
or the fight analogies that are sometimes

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.850
used, maybe it makes it more relatable.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.650
Maybe it just makes it more confusing to people.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.170
Let me know what you think.

